00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.210
what is the
importance of features

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:23.280
in regards to machine
learning and why do we

00:23:23.280 --> 00:23:24.870
need to do feature engineering?

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:26.190
Like, why is that a thing?

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:27.814
MELANIE WARRICK: So
feature engineering

00:23:27.814 --> 00:23:30.110
has been something that spent
a priority to developing

00:23:30.110 --> 00:23:32.790
models in machine learning,
and it's required a lot of work

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:33.790
in the past.

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:37.530
Particularly, it's used to
help drive out or define

00:23:37.530 --> 00:23:39.030
specific attributes
of properties

00:23:39.030 --> 00:23:41.310
about the data set that
doesn't necessarily

00:23:41.310 --> 00:23:42.600
come across with raw data.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:44.370
And it helps you
identify what's more

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:47.550
important to help drive the
predictive models that you're

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:48.450
building.

00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:50.100
Like I said, it's
something that has

00:23:50.100 --> 00:23:51.960
required a lot of manual
labor in the past.

00:23:51.960 --> 00:23:56.070
It can play a large role
in terms of the preparation

00:23:56.070 --> 00:23:57.990
or lead up to developing models.

00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:00.480
But with deep learning
becoming such a popular thing

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.850
in the last few years, feature
engineering in particular

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:06.000
has become something that
we see as being automated

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:07.260
through deep learning.

00:24:07.260 --> 00:24:08.760
But the reality
is, it's not fully

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:09.690
automated through deep learning.

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:11.148
It's definitely
one of those things

00:24:11.148 --> 00:24:15.780
that is still necessary to
do some level of analysis,

00:24:15.780 --> 00:24:16.560
so to speak.

00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:19.020
So it's good that Dataprep
is providing that opportunity

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:21.830
to be able to help with the
feature engineering process.

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:23.700
But yeah, that's
what it's useful for.

